-- title:
--   Unramifiedness over the X₀(q²M') floor at an Igusa cusp, q=3
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime with $q = 3$, let $M'$ be a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$, and let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is algebraic over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $K$ be the intermediate field of $L \subseteq \operatorname{LaurentSeries} L$ obtained as [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103) of [`ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') (ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M')`](def/ModularCurve_XH.html#L79), that is, the subfield of $L((t))$ generated over $L$ by the image of the rational $X_H$-function field of level $q^2M'$ under the coefficientwise map [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) induced by $\mathbb{Q} \to L$, the subgroup `levelH q M'` of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times$ being the kernel of the map of unit groups attached to the divisibility `dvd_sq_mul q M'`. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation ring with fraction field $L$, whose maximal ideal contains $q$ and is generated by $\varpi$, with $K$ an $A$-algebra compatibly with $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero with image in $L((t))$ equal to the image of the $q$-expansion [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) $= t^{-1}\cdot(\text{power series } \mathtt{jNumQ})$, and let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $K$ consisting exactly of those $f$ admitting power series $x, y$ over $A$ with $y$ having nonzero reduction modulo the maximal ideal and $f \cdot y = x$ in $L((t))$. Let $K_2$ be the corresponding base change to $L$ of the $q$-expansion function field [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) of $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$, assumed contained in $K$. Let $w$ be a place of $K$ over $L$ (a proper valuation subring containing $L$ whose ideals are principal) with $w.\mathrm{ord}$ of $j^{-1}$, taken in the subalgebra `chartAlgInf` of elements of $K$ integral over $A[j^{-1}]$, strictly positive; and let $y$ be a maximal ideal of that subalgebra containing $\varpi$, containing every element whose image in $K$ is a nonunit of $W_0$, and containing every element of strictly positive $w$-order. Then the ramification index along the inclusion $K_2 \hookrightarrow K$ at $w$, that is the least positive $n$ of the form $w.\mathrm{ord}(f)$ for some nonzero $f \in K_2$, equals $1$.
--
--   This asserts that a place of the function field of $X_H(q^2M')$ lying over the vanishing locus of $1/j$ and specialising into a closed point of the pole chart on the $\infty$-Igusa branch cut out by $W_0$ is unramified over the intermediate floor given by $\Gamma_0(q^2M')$; it is the $q = 3$ case of a statement whose remaining cases are treated separately. It feeds the corresponding unramifiedness statement for the full inclusion used in the analysis of cusps on the Igusa tower.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_FullLevel_ramificationIndexAlong_inclusion_gamma0_sq_mul_eq_one_of_ord_jInvChartInf_pos_of_forall_mem_nonunits_gauss_xH_of_eq_three.lean

